{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And she called his name Moshe.</b> And if you ask: but she was Egyptian, so how did she call [him] in the Hebrew language? The answer is that she called him a name in the Egyptian language whose meaning is Moshe, and the Torah called him Moshe in the Hebrew language. Another explanation: she learned the Hebrew language from when the Hebrew women came to Egypt. And so we find that Pharaoh called Yosef's name Tzafenat Paneach."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:03:07.489918307Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}